.TH FREE 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
free \- display amount of free and used memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display total, used, free, and available memory and swap.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Reads Linux's /proc; on any other target this returns a clear "not available on this target" error rather than guessing or returning zeroes -- mitosOS does not expose an equivalent interface yet, see mitos-utils-integration(7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if unavailable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
